---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EmailSignup from '../components/EmailSignup.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="What UAP Times is, and the editorial standard we hold ourselves to.">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="article-header prose">
      <h1>About UAP Times</h1>
      <p class="lede">Serious reporting on an unserious-sounding subject.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="article-body prose">
      <p>
        UAP Times covers unidentified anomalous phenomena — UFOs, if you're
        feeling old-fashioned — the way any other news beat should be covered:
        with sources, scepticism, and a clear line between what's known and
        what's merely claimed.
      </p>
      <h5>Our editorial standard</h5>
      <p>
        We don't debunk for sport and we don't believe for sport either. Every
        story carries a credibility rating so you always know how much weight the
        evidence actually bears. A government sensor log and a blurry phone video
        are not the same thing, and we won't pretend they are.
      </p>
      <h5>How we work</h5>
      <p>
        Stories are researched and drafted with AI assistance and reviewed by a
        human before publication. We think that's the honest way to run a modern
        newsroom, and we'd rather tell you than have you guess.
      </p>
      <h5>Got a tip?</h5>
      <p>
        Seen something? Sat on a document? Email
        <a href="mailto:tips@uaptimes.com">tips@uaptimes.com</a>.
        Anonymity respected.
      </p>
    </div>
    <EmailSignup />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
